 "response": "Likror's current budget is **$2,632K**.\n\n**Approach**\n- Only Finance Office budget entries count. The vendor, sales, PMO, engineering and other messages were ignored.\n- Finance Office entries that don't change the budget were also skipped. These include invoice archives, receipts, audits, room moves and cost center changes.\n- For each withdrawal chain, I worked back from the last withdrawal that nothing else withdraws, alternating \"in effect\" and \"cancelled\" down the chain.\n\n**Decisive chains**\n- **#0013:** #0279 withdraws #0113, which revives #0022. #0022 cancels #0021, which revives #0016. #0016 withdraws #0013. So #0013 is out.\n- **#0003:** #0340 cancels #0332, which revives #0168. #0168 cancels #0105, which revives #0051. #0051 cancels #0027. So #0003 stands.\n- **Other updates that stand:** #0036, #0007, #0010, #0024, #0110, #0055, #0180, #0044, #0208, #0141, #0330, #0469, #0700, #0646, #0902, #0781, #0470 and #1075.\n- **Other updates that are out:** #0008, #0089, #0045, #0085, #0145, #0252, #0128, #0696, #0384 and #0835.\n- About 120 budget updates are withdrawn in total; every other Finance Office update applies once.\n\n**Calculation**\nStarting from $2,090K (#0001), I applied every remaining Finance Office update in record order. The running total ends at $2,632K after #1599. I did this once and did not run a separate second check.\n\nANSWER: $2632K",
